@startuml state-llm-request
title Life cycle of an LLMRequest

[*] --> Pending : stage attaches request\n(classical decision already applied)

Pending --> Skipped : LLM disabled or\nOllama unreachable
Pending --> CacheLookup : stage 7 starts batch\nfor the request's model

CacheLookup --> Resolved : cache hit
CacheLookup --> Sent : cache miss

Sent --> Resolved : valid answer\n/ store in cache
Sent --> Retrying : invalid answer\nor timeout

Retrying --> Resolved : valid answer\n/ store in cache
Retrying --> Fallback : invalid again

Resolved : status = RESOLVED
Resolved : answer replaces classical decision
Resolved : provenance(used_llm = true)

Skipped : status = SKIPPED
Skipped : classical decision stands

Fallback : status = FALLBACK
Fallback : classical decision stands
Fallback : provenance note with the error

Resolved --> [*]
Skipped --> [*]
Fallback --> [*]

note right of CacheLookup
  key = hash(model, prompt version, payload)
  Same input and prompt version
  give the same answer across runs.
end note
@enduml
